OL,3,ABurnham 'open' to calls for slavery
OL,4,Aapology but not reparations
OL,5,
OL,6,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham has said he
OL,7,Fis "open" to the possibility of the UK
OL,8,Fissuing a formal apology for its role
OL,9,Fin the transatlantic slave trade, but
OL,10,Fhas ruled out considering financial
OL,11,Freparations.
OL,13,FBurham said he wanted a "dialogue with
OL,14,Fthose affected by the slave trade" and
OL,15,Fwas open to "calls for an apology".
OL,17,FHe dismissed the idea of paying
OL,18,Ffinancial reparations, saying they were
OL,19,F"not the right answer".
OL,23,APub: 31-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,0,100
